== Free Threading

PEP 703 makes the GIL optional in CPython @PEP703, allowing Python threads to execute bytecode concurrently in a free-threaded build. We use free-threaded CPython (`3.15t`) to test whether threads can reduce the process and inter-process communication overhead of the existing parallel implementation @PyFreeThreadingGuide. We extended that implementation to use Python's `threading` module when the GIL is disabled, while retaining multiprocessing on GIL-enabled builds. This keeps the existing workflow interface and lets us compare worker models without changing the ETL program.

For the evaluation, CPython was built with `--disable-gil` to enable free-threading, as well as `--enable-optimizations` and `--with-lto` @Python315ConfigureDocs. These build options are held constant for the free-threaded runs.